  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "VRChat Version: 2022.2.1\nDescription of the bug:\nThe SDK documentation says that the allowable range of a float parameter is -1.0..1.0, but the allowable range of a IEEE 32-bit float value is much much larger. OSC allows sending any IEEE float value, and VRChat will accept any value and assign that value directly to the animator parameter.\nThis means a user with OSC input will see their avatar incorrectly. Most likely, they will see their avatar how they intended it to look, but everybody else will see something different.\nSteps to reproduce:\n1. Create an avatar that has a synchronized OSC float parameter.\n2. Create an animator that responds to the float parameter being greater than 2.0 (or some other value strictly greater than 1.0).\n3. Use OSC to set the float parameter and trigger the animation.\nYou can also see the illegal value in the debug window.",
